    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the city-capacity rule: creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nKept structural impact minimal by adding small, cohesive new units rather than modifying existing methods \u2014 every changed function is a brand-new class with a single method (so `WMC_other` = 0 \u2192 1, and no existing class grew):\n\n**New files:**\n- `EnsureOwnerCityWithinCapacity.java` \u2014 one step that counts owners in the same city (case-insensitively, matching the existing household normalization) and throws when `>= 50`.\n- `CityAtCapacityException.java` \u2014 checked exception.\n- `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409, reusing the existing `ProblemDetails` builder pattern.\n- `...CityAtCapacityException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring.\n\n**Edited (1 file):**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `ensureCityCapacity` step after the household check.\n\nThe existing `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique` and its handler were left untouched.",
